-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

WHY THIS LICENCE

The audited tree contained no licence at all (F-065). That is not a neutral
state: default copyright applies, but nobody can tell whether that was intended,
and a store reviewer, a collaborator or a buyer has no answer to "what am I
allowed to do with this?".

Proprietary, all rights reserved, is the settled decision and matches the
product: Ciyato is a commercial application being prepared for release on Google
Play, with the launcher, organizer, file management and photo tooling as paid or
paid-adjacent capability. A permissive licence would be the wrong instrument for
that, and it cannot be withdrawn afterwards — anyone who obtained the code under
one keeps those rights permanently.
